324557aa-aca6-4b85-9696-5374bced6f1d	578bf880-bf63-4433-bb10-2b50ebcaf97f	assistant	Bravo Ines (PC 03)! You built the full Compte contract and cloning skeleton — solid start.\n\nThink of Compte like Slide 29's bank/e-wallet contract: adding transferer as abstract forces every class to rewrite it, breaking teams. Java 8 solves this with default giving shared behavior automatically, and static utilities living in the interface itself. Marker Cloneable works differently: empty, just permission for Object.clone(), otherwise CloneNotSupportedException.\n\nWhy do you think making transferer default instead of abstract lets CompteBancaire inherit it with no extra code?	{"label": "Chapter 5 (Slide 49): Default evolution and interface rigidity", "en_note": "Default methods allow evolving Compte with transferer without breaking CompteBancaire; static helpers and Cloneable marker complete the picture.", "pdf_url": "https://peddvhsykuglvicfaezr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-pdfs/java_oop/chapters/ch5_interfaces_v4.pdf", "page_number": 49, "chapter_code": "CH5_INTERFACES_V4", "slide_markdown": {"en": "### Default Methods - default Keyword\\n#### Solution\\n- To partially overcome this problem, an interface can provide a default implementation of its methods.\\n- Thus, if a concrete class that implements this interface does not implement a default method, it is the code of the interface that will be executed.\\n- A default method must obligatorily have the default keyword in its signature.\\n```java\\npublic interface Compte {\\n    default void transferer(Compte autre, double montant) {\\n        // default implementation\\n    }\\n}\\n```", "fr": "### Méthodes par défaut - Mot-clé default\\n#### Solution\\n- Pour palier partiellement à ce problème, une interface peut fournir une implémentation par défaut de ses méthodes.\\n- Ainsi, si une classe concrète qui implémente cette interface n’implémente pas une méthode par défaut, c’est le code de l’interface qui s’exécutera.\\n- Une méthode par défaut doit obligatoirement avoir le mot-clé default dans sa signature.\\n```java\\npublic interface Compte {\\n    default void transferer(Compte autre, double montant) {\\n        // implémentation par défaut\\n    }\\n}\\n```"}}	[{"name": "Compte.java", "content": "public interface Compte {\\n  void deposer(int montant);\\n  int retirer(int montant);\\n  int getBalance();\\n  void transferer(Compte destination);\\n}"}, {"name": "CompteBancaire.java", "content": "public class CompteBancaire implements Compte {\\n  private int balance;\\n  public void deposer(int montant) { balance += montant; }\\n  public int retirer(int montant) { balance -= montant; return montant; }\\n  public int getBalance() { return balance; }\\n  public void transferer(Compte destination) {\\n    destination.deposer(100);\\n  }\\n}"}, {"name": "TestClone.java", "content": "public class TestClone {\\n  int value = 10;\\n  public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {\\n    return super.clone();\\n  }\\n}"}]	9896	2026-11-02 10:15:42.25536+00	act_1
